 "integration": {
  "summary": "Enable Modbus RTU with ID 2208 = 1 (Modbus TCP is always on), set Remote control place ID 172 = 1, then write FB control word 2001 (1 = run) and FB speed reference 2003 (0-10000 = 0-100 % of min-max frequency) and poll 2101-2111 for status, actual speed, frequency, current and fault code. Every register number in the manual is 1-based: subtract 1 on the wire.",
  "minimum_registers": [
   {
    "table": "holding_register",
    "address": 2000,
    "why": "FB control word: run, direction, fault reset"
   },
   {
    "table": "holding_register",
    "address": 2002,
    "why": "FB speed reference, 0.01 % of min-max range"
   },
   {
    "table": "holding_register",
    "address": 2100,
    "why": "FB status word: ready/run/fault/alarm"
   },
   {
    "table": "holding_register",
    "address": 2103,
    "why": "Output frequency, 0.01 Hz"
   },
   {
    "table": "holding_register",
    "address": 44,
    "why": "Motor current, 0.1 A (ID 45)"
   },
   {
    "table": "holding_register",
    "address": 2109,
    "why": "DC link voltage"
   },
   {
    "table": "holding_register",
    "address": 2110,
    "why": "Active fault code"
   },
   {
    "table": "holding_register",
    "address": 171,
    "why": "ID 172 remote control place (1 = fieldbus)"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "Modbus RTU: set P5.8.1.1 RS-485 protocol (ID 2208) = Modbus RTU, after which its settings appear under P5.8.3 (slave address ID 2320, baud ID 2378, parity ID 2379, stop bits ID 2380, time-out ID 2321). Modbus TCP/UDP is always enabled; set the IP mode and address under P5.9.1. For control set Remote control place P3.2.1 (ID 172) = Fieldbus control, Local/remote (ID 211) = Remote, and leave Fieldbus control reference selection (ID 122) = 3 Fieldbus. Control word bits 8/9 can also force fieldbus control and reference.",
  "watchdog": "RTU: ID 2321 communication time-out (seconds, default 10, 0 = off). TCP/UDP: ID 2448 time-out (seconds, default 10); a connection can also set its own timeout at register 40501. The reaction is ID 733 Response to fieldbus communication fault (default 3 = fault, stop per stop function); the fault is code 53 Fieldbus communication fault.",
  "quirks": [
   "The manual's register numbers are 1-based: control word 2001 goes on the wire as 2000 (07D0h), as the manual's own write example shows; ID n is wire n-1.",
   "16-bit process data at 2001/2101 carries only the low half of the 32-bit control and status words; the full words are at 2051-2052 and 2151-2152, high word first.",
   "FB speed reference and FB actual speed are 0-10000 = 0-100.00 % of the min-to-max frequency span, not Hz (manual example: 5000 = 25.00 Hz with 0-50 Hz limits).",
   "Holding and input registers return the same data at the same address; coils and discrete inputs (control/status bits) work on Modbus TCP/UDP only.",
   "TCP unit identifier defaults to 255 and is checked on TCP as well as UDP."
  ],
  "setup": [
   "RS-485 on the standard terminal block terminals A and B (A = negative, B = positive); ground the cable shield with the supplied clamp.",
   "Set the RS-485 termination DIP switch (next to the keypad) to ON on the first and last device on the bus; biasing is built into the termination.",
   "RTU defaults: slave address 1, 9600 baud, even parity; 300 to 230400 baud supported.",
   "Ethernet: DHCP by default; switching to Fixed gives 192.168.0.10 / 255.255.0.0 / gateway 192.168.0.1. Up to three Modbus TCP/UDP connections.",
   "UDP is supported from firmware FW0072V025 (INDUSTRIAL / 100 X), FW0159V016 (FLOW) and FW0065V035 (HVAC); use UDP for cyclic process data and TCP for parameter reads/writes."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "Updating the control unit firmware restores defaults, which usually puts the control place back to I/O.",
   "Unused control word bits must be written as 0; on 100 HVAC bits 5, 7 and 10-12 are not supported.",
